1 Introduction
Road transport safety is a significant issue. Human factors have been determined to be the primary cause of more than 90% of accidents, thus the implementation of modern technology, including autonomous vehicles, is a potential means of minimising the risk of human error. The utilisation of autonomous technologies is poised to displace the conventional role of the driver, thereby mitigating incidents attributable to driver inattention and distraction [1, 2]. While it is improbable that full automation will replace human drivers entirely in the coming decades [3], a shift towards mixed traffic is expected.
